;; The config (session CONFIG, owner 2026-10-21: "the only things that should stay are documented
;; config schemas that we are porting from seon if they are relevant"). The values, with each
;; key's unit, provenance and what happens at its bound, are in resources/seon/config/default.edn;
;; the keys' schemas are in seon.config.<area>.edn, v1's shape (~/src/seon resources/seon/schemas/
;; seon.config.*.edn): a schema with a :description and its :seon.config/unit.
;;
;; :seon.config/config is the whole resolved config: open, as every entity schema is (root's entity holds it beside
;; root's own facts), and every key optional, since a task holds single keys as its overrides; a write is held to the
;; keys it holds. The loader closes it at its top (seon.config's `closed`), so an unknown key refuses boot; that the
;; shipped file states every key is seon.config-test/the-shipped-file-validates-under-every-profile's,
;; and its entries declare the attributes root writes on main's root entity (seon.config/facts).
{:seon.config/config
 [:map {:seon.db/attributes true :seon.render/hiccup seon.render.ui/config-panel
        :description "The resolved config: every limit, bound and default of the platform, one key each."}
